Implement enable_gearing_parallel as DP mode
===========================================

Decisions applied
-----------------
- Rename flag to `enable_gearing_parallel`.
- Use `enable_gearing_parallel` for DP behavior (different requests per rank).
- Use Python assignment rule exactly: `hash(req_id) % cp_size == cp_rank`.

Code changes
------------
1) arctic_inference/vllm/args.py
- Updated CLI flag to `--enable-gearing-parallel` and help text to describe DP sharding + executor merge behavior.

2) arctic_inference/vllm/config.py
- Added `ArcticParallelConfig.gearing_parallel_size` property:
  - returns `ulysses_sequence_parallel_size` when `enable_gearing_parallel` is true
  - returns 1 otherwise

3) arctic_inference/vllm/ulysses.py
- Extended `UlyssesMultiprocExecutor` with:
  - `_CPAllDPOutputAggregator` to integrate with `collective_rpc`.
  - `_merge_cp_outputs(outputs)` to combine per-rank `ModelRunnerOutput`s into one:
    - merges `req_ids`
    - rebuilds `req_id_to_index`
    - merges `sampled_token_ids`, `logprobs`, `prompt_logprobs_dict`
    - sums `num_nans_in_logits`
    - forwards `_actual_draft_lens` metadata if present
  - `execute_model(...)` override:
    - normal path unchanged when flag is off
    - when flag is on, sets `unique_reply_rank=None` and merges all worker outputs
  - `sample_tokens(...)` override with the same all-worker merge behavior

4) arctic_inference/vllm/model_runner.py
- In `GPUModelRunnerPatch.__init__`, added:
  - `cp_all_dp_enabled`
  - `cp_all_dp_size`
  - `cp_all_dp_rank`
  - `_cp_all_dp_owned_req_ids` tracking set
- In `execute_model(...)`, added pre-filter step:
  - `scheduler_output = _filter_scheduler_output_for_cp_dp(...)` when DP mode is enabled
- Added `_filter_scheduler_output_for_cp_dp(...)`:
  - shallow-copies scheduler output
  - filters `scheduled_new_reqs` and `scheduled_cached_reqs` by rank ownership
  - conditionally filters `scheduled_running_reqs` when field exists
  - filters `num_scheduled_tokens` and recomputes `total_num_scheduled_tokens`
  - filters `finished_req_ids` using owned-ids tracking plus hash fallback
  - filters `scheduled_spec_decode_tokens`, `scheduled_encoder_inputs`
  - filters `pending_structured_output_tokens` (if dict)
  - filters `preempted_req_ids`

Notes
-----
- This is intentionally first-step DP only under one scheduler.
- Existing attention/model-config gating on `enable_gearing_parallel` remains active (skip all-to-all path).
